            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "\\( 2^{x} \\) is an exponential function with a constant base, so its derivative is \\( 2^{x} \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)} \\); the power rule does not apply to it.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Multiply",
            [
               "Power",
               2,
               "x"
            ],
            [
               "Ln",
               2
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "The factor \\( \\sin^{2}(3x) \\) is a square of \\( \\sin(3x) \\), which is a sine of \\( 3x \\), so apply the chain rule from the outside inward: \\( \\left(\\sin^{2}(3x)\\right)' = 6 \\sin{\\left(3 x \\right)} \\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Multiply",
